cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Disproof of the lower-bound conjecture in OEIS A398786, with the smallest counterexample located at n = 90"
authors:
  - name: "ZL"
date-released: 2026-10-03
version: "1.0.0"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MakiseKurisu816/A398786-conjecture-disproof"
keywords:
  - OEIS
  - A398786
  - A091508
  - integer sequences
  - counterexample
  - number theory
abstract: >
  OEIS A398786 counts the starting values m for which the Cloitre map A091508 first
  reaches 1 at step n. The entry conjectures a(n) >= prod_{k=2..n}(d(k)-1). This
  repository contains exact-integer certificates showing the conjecture is false
  (a(90) < P(90), a(120) < P(120), and a(n) < P(n) for 120 <= n <= 300), certificates
  that it holds for n <= 44, fifteen new exact terms a(26)..a(40), and unbiased
  importance-sampled estimates locating the smallest counterexample at n = 90.
